# Tailwind: use IDE shorthand suggestions

When Tailwind CSS IntelliSense or the linter says a class **can be written as**
a shorter form, apply that suggestion. Do not leave the verbose form.

## Do this

- Prefer the suggested class over the longer arbitrary variant.
- Apply the rewrite while editing, not as a follow-up unless you only spotted it
  in review.
- If several classes in the same string have suggestions, fix all of them.

## Examples

| Verbose                 | Prefer          |
| ----------------------- | --------------- |
| `[&_:first-child]:mt-0` | `**:first:mt-0` |
| `[&_:last-child]:mb-0`  | `**:last:mb-0`  |

Same rule for any other `can be written as …` Tailwind diagnostic the IDE shows.

## Scope

- Applies to `className`, `class`, `@apply`, and `cn(...)` / similar helpers.
- Do not invent shorthands the tooling did not suggest.
- Unrelated arbitrary variants with no IDE suggestion may stay as-is.
